t/11094580/"}}, "issued": {"date-parts": [[2025, 6, 10]]}, "references-count": 0, "URL": "https://doi.org/10.1109/cvpr52734.2025.01325", "published": {"date-parts": [[2025, 6, 10]]}}, {"indexed": {"date-parts": [[2026, 7, 8]], "date-time": "2026-07-08T13:14:11Z", "timestamp": 1783516451888, "version": "3.55.0"}, "publisher": "Publications Office of the European Union", "award": "101175984", "DOI": "10.3030/101175984", "type": "grant", "created": {"date-parts": [[2025, 7, 9]], "date-time": "2025-07-09T11:48:49Z", "timestamp": 1752061729000}, "source": "Crossref", "prefix": "10.3030", "member": "4854", "project": [{"project-title": [{"title": "RudolfVX: A multimodal foundation model for pathology to power precision medicine with human centric generative AI", "language": "en"}, {"title": "RudolfVX", "language": "en"}], "project-description": [{"description": "The convergence of artificial intelligence with the growing abundance of medical data has the potential to revolutionize the medical landscape. The shift to precision medicine is currently hindered by a lack of technological advancements and integration of diverse medical data. \nAignostics, a spin-off from Charit\u00e9 Berlin, is developing RudolfVX - a large-scale multimodal foundation model for pathology, capable of leading the way to improved disease diagnosis, better therapy decisions and accelerated drug development. Emerging as the first of its kind in the EU, this sophisticated AI model is capable of creating valuable insights from multiple data types including clinical reports, omics data, and medical images. The model leverages artificial neural networks and self-supervised learning, minimizing data annotation limitations and optimizing computational efficiency. RudolfVX is set to transform pathology and healthcare by integrating generative AI solutions with a human-centric focus, pioneering new possibilities in the field. These downstream applications will stem from a transparent model, fully compliant with EU values in the AI domain. Our solution will enable improved patient outcomes, reduced healthcare costs, and will address the high failure rates in traditional drug development. With RudolfVX, Aignostics will strengthen Europe\u2019s position and become a market leader in computational pathology, offering significant potential in precision medicine and healthcare advancements.", "language": "en"}], "award-amount": {"amount": 2499999.0, "currency": "EUR"}, "funding": [{"type": "grant", "scheme": "HORIZON.3.1", "award-amount": {"amount": 2499999.0, "currency": "EUR", "percentage": 100}, "funder": {"id": [{"id": "10.13039/100018703", "id-type": "DOI", "asserted-by": "publisher"}], "name": "HORIZON EUROPE HORIZON.3.1"}}]}], "deposited": {"date-parts": [[2026, 7, 8]], "date-time": "2026-07-08T12:19:50Z", "timestamp": 1783513190000}, "score": 27.712683, "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "https://cordis.europa.eu/project/id/101175984"}}, "issued": {"date-parts": [[null]]}, "URL": "https://doi.org/10.3030/101175984"}, {"indexed": {"date-parts": [[2026, 9, 3]], "date-time": "2026-09-03T01:28:40Z", "timestamp": 1788398920568, "version": "build-2803163510"}, "reference-count": 4, "publisher": "Massachusetts Medical Society", "issue": "12", "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "short-container-title": ["NEJM AI"], "published-print": {"date-parts": [[2024, 11, 27]]}, "DOI": "10.1056/aie2401024", "type": "journal-article", "created": {"date-parts": [[2024, 11, 27]], "date-time": "2024-11-27T14:00:28Z", "timestamp": 1732716028000}, "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 8, "title": ["A New Foundation Model for Multimodal Ophthalmic Images: Advancing Disease Detection and Prediction"], "prefix": "10.1056", "volume": "1", "author": [{"ORCID": "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0339-5186", "authenticated-orcid": false, "given": "Mark A.", "family": "Chia", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [{"name": "University College London"}, {"name": "Moorfie