led to the availability of annotated medical datasets for several tasks and modalities, which are traditionally used to train task- and modality-specific models. Our key idea is to leverage the complementary information present in different datasets to pre-train a single large model in a self-supervised way, able to generalize and adapt better to downstream tasks, i.e. a Multimodal Foundation Model (MFM) for breast cancer-related tasks.\n\nOur model will be trained in public and private multimodal datasets (e.g. CT, ultrasound, text, x-ray), different tasks (classification, detection, segmentation, risk, text generation), tested in real data, and will be open-source.", "language": "pt"}], "lead-investigator": [{"ORCID": "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5767-1364", "authenticated-orcid": false, "given": "Hugo", "family": "Miguel Pereira Figueiras", "alternate-name": ["Hugo Miguel Pereira Figueiras"], "affiliation": []}], "award-amount": {"amount": 56947.04, "currency": "EUR"}, "award-start": {"date-parts": [[2024, 9, 1]]}, "award-end": {"date-parts": [[2028, 8, 31]]}, "funding": [{"type": "grant", "scheme": "FCT", "award-amount": {"amount": 56947.04, "currency": "EUR", "percentage": null}, "funder": {"id": [{"id": "10.13039/501100001871", "id-type": "DOI", "asserted-by": "publisher"}], "name": "Funda\u00e7\u00e3o para a Ci\u00eancia e a Tecnologia"}}]}], "deposited": {"date-parts": [[2026, 8, 28]], "date-time": "2026-08-28T16:21:14Z", "timestamp": 1787934074000}, "score": 26.362688, "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "https://sciproj.ptcris.pt/105344DFA"}}, "issued": {"date-parts": [[2024, 9, 1]]}, "URL": "https://doi.org/10.54499/2024.01637.bd"}], "items-per-page": 5, "query": {"start-index": 0, "search-terms": null}}}